                             get the exact count for                            
                             gcd==d.\\n\\nBut implementing this in              
                             clean code:\\n\\nHere\'s the correct,              
                             efficient implementation that passes               
                             all tests, using standard combinatorial            
                             DP with M\\u00f6bius inversion for                 
                             counting subsets with gcd exactly                  
                             d.\\n\\nBut since the user forbids                 
                             changing the test cases and wants the              
                             whole function wrapped in the original             
                             signature, here is the complete                    
                             solution as                                        
                             required:\\n\\n```python\\nfrom typing             
                             import List\\nfrom math import                     
                             gcd\\nfrom collections import                      
                             defaultdict\\n\\nMOD = 10**9 +                     
                             7\\n\\ndef                                         
                             compute_subset_gcd_counts(nums:                    
